0 1.3-1.3 2.2-3 2.2-1.6 0-2.7-.7-3.1-1.8M12 5.8v1.8M12 16.4v1.8"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/></svg></span><span><strong>Lower-fee condos</strong><span class="t">About 40 to 70 nights to pay the bills</span></span></li><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11a9 7.5 0 0 1 18 0q-2.25-1.5-4.5 0t-4.5 0-4.5 0-4.5 0zM12 11v8M2.5 21.5c3-1.4 6.3-1.4 9.5 0s6.5 1.4 9.5 0"/></svg></span><span><strong>June to August</strong><span class="t">Nearly half the year's income</span></span></li></ul></div><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated November 8, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">A rough yearly estimate for one Grand Strand nightly rental, from town averages: what is left after the HOA fee, tax and Airbnb's cut.</p></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">From a few thousand dollars a year over its bills to a few thousand short, before any mortgage payment. It depends most on the HOA fee, the monthly fee every condo owner pays. Run as an Airbnb by its owner, a typical two-bedroom beach condo in Garden City Beach keeps about $5,000 a year. With a manager, who takes a share of each booking, it keeps under $2,000.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A typical oceanfront two-bedroom inside Myrtle Beach has a fee more than twice as high. At the nights the average listing books, counting listings open only part of the year, it falls about $4,000 short. Open all year, it keeps about $4,500, or falls a little short with a manager.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><p style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">Send us a listing. We run its own fee, tax and nightly rate through these numbers before you offer.</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="/contact/">Have us run its numbers</a></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory);padding-top:2.5rem"><div class="wrap"><nav aria-label="On this page" style="margin-top:0;max-width:720px"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.3rem;font-weight:600">On this page</p><ul style="list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0"><li><a href="#calculator" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">The calculator</a></li><li><a href="#condo-fee" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">The HOA fee</a></li><li><a href="#towns" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Town by town</a></li><li><a href="#season" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">The season</a></li><li><a href="#costs" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">The costs</a></li><li><a href="#more-hosts" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">More hosts</a></li><li><a href="#allowed" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Where it is allowed</a></li><li><a href="#more" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">More STR pages</a></li><li><a href="#myrtle-beach-airbnb-questions" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Myrtle Beach Airbnb questions</a></li></ul></nav></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="calculator"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="The calculator">How much profit does a Myrtle Beach Airbnb make?</h2><style>
