role="rowheader"><span class="n"><a href="/submarkets/little-river/">Little River</a></span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.423" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$12,000</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>Money from guests, cleaning fees included, before any cost. AirROI's market areas, 12 months to September 2026. Little River and Conway have few two-bedroom listings.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Counting all sizes, Murrells Inlet's average Airbnb took in nearly twice Myrtle Beach's. Most of Murrells Inlet's listings are houses, and most of its homes sleep groups. Four in five of Myrtle Beach's listings are condos, and Myrtle Beach has far more listings than any other town here.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Torn between two towns?</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send us a listing in each. We run both through the same numbers, at no cost.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Send us two listings</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="season"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="The season">How slow is the off season for a Myrtle Beach Airbnb?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A Myrtle Beach Airbnb earns about five times as much in July as in January, when the ocean is about 50 degrees. June, July and August bring in nearly half its year. In Murrells Inlet, where most Airbnbs are houses, they bring 43 percent.</p><figure class="st-mo"><p class="cap" id="stMoCap">What the average Airbnb earns each month, with the ocean's temperature</p><div class="st-key" aria-hidden="true"><span><i></i><span><b>Myrtle Beach</b>, mostly condos</span></span><span><i class="mi"></i><span><b>Murrells Inlet</b>, mostly houses</span></span></div><div role="table" aria-labelledby="stMoCap"><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row" class="hd"><span role="columnheader">Month, ocean</span><span role="columnheader"><span class="sr">Bars</span></span><span role="columnheader" style="text-align:right">Earned</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader">Jan<span class="sr">uary</span><small>50°F</small></span><span role="cell" class="bars"><span class="b" style="--f:0.137" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="b mi" style="--f:0.23" aria-hidden="true"></span></span><span role="cell" class="v"><span><span class="sr">Myrtle Beach </span>$1,300</span><span><span class="sr">Murrells Inlet </span>$2,300</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader">Feb<span class="sr">ruary</span><small>52°F</small></span><span role="cell" class="bars"><span class="b" style="--f:0.172" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="b mi" style="--f:0.272" aria-hidden="true"></span></span><span role="cell" class="v"><span><span class="sr">Myrtle Beach </span>$1,700</span><span><span class="sr">Murrells Inlet </span>$2,700</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader">Mar<span class="sr">ch</span><small>59°F</small></span><span role="cell" class="bars"><span class="b" style="--f:0.259" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="b mi" style="--f:0.441" aria-hidden="true"></span></span><span role="cell" class="v"><span><span class="sr">Myrtle Beach </span>$2,500</span><span><span class="sr">Murrells Inlet </span>$4,300</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader">Apr<span class="sr">il</span><small>67°F</small></span><span role="cell" class="bars"><span class="b" style="--f:0.286" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="b mi" style="--f:0.534" aria-hidden="true"></span></span><span role="cell" class="v"><span><span class="sr">Myrtle Beach </span>$2,800</span><span><span class="sr">Murrells Inlet </span>$5,200</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader">May<span class="sr"></span><small>74°F</small></span><span role="cell" class="bars"><span class="b" style="--f:0.334" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="b mi" style="--f:0.617" aria-hidden="true"></span></span><span role="cell" class="v"><span><span class="sr">Myrtle Beach </span>$3,300</span><span><span class="sr">Murrells Inlet </span>$6,000</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader">Jun<span class="sr">e</span><small>79°F</small></span><span role="cell" class="bars"><span class="b" style="--f:0.621" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="b mi" style="--f:0.951" aria-hidden="true"></span></span><span role="cell" class="v"><span><span class="sr">Myrtle Beach </span>$6,100</span><span><span class="sr">Murrells Inlet </span>$9,300</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader">Jul<span class="sr">y</span><small>84°F</small></span><span role="cell" class="bars"><span class="b" style="--f:0.695" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="b mi" style="--f:1" aria-hidden="true"></span></span><span role="cell" class="v"><span><span class="sr">Myrtle Beach </span>$6,800</span><span><span class="sr">Murrells Inlet </span>$9,800</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader">Aug<span class="sr">ust</span><small>84°F</small></span><span role="cell" class="bars"><span class="b" style="--f:0.45" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="b mi" style="--f:0.699" aria-hidden="true"></span></span><span role="cell" class="v"><span><span class="sr">Myrtle Beach </span>$4,400</span><span><span class="sr">Murrells Inlet </span>$6,800</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader">Sep<span class="sr">tember</span><small>80°F</small></span><span role="cell" class="bars"><span class="b" style="--f:0.261" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="b mi" style="--f:0.459" aria-hidden="true"></span></span><span role="cell" class="v"><span><span class="sr">Myrtle Beach </span>$2,600</span><span><span class="sr">Murrells Inlet </span>$4,500</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader">Oct<span class="sr">ober</span><small>72°F</small></span><span role="cell" class="bars"><span class="b" style="--f:0.22" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="b mi" style="--f:0.399" aria-hidden="true"></span></span><span role="cell" class="v"><span><span class="sr">Myrtle Beach </span>$2,200</span><span><span class="sr">Murrells Inlet </span>$3,900</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader">Nov<span class="sr">ember</span><small>64°F</small></span><span role="cell" class="bars"><span class="b" style="--f:0.166" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="b mi" style="--f:0.309" aria-hidden="true"></span></span><span role="cell" class="v"><span><span class="sr">Myrtle Beach </span>$1,600</span><span><span class="sr">Murrells Inlet </span>$3,000</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader">Dec<span class="sr">ember</span><small>54°F</small></span><span role="cell" class="bars"><span class="b" style="--f:0.163" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="b mi" style="--f:0.305" aria-hidden="true"></span></span><span role="cell" class="v"><span><span class="sr">Myrtle Beach </span>$1,600</span><span><span class="sr">Murrells Inlet </span>$3,000</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>Average money from guests per Airbnb listing open that month, over the last two years (AirROI). Ocean: the average water temperature at NOAA's Springmaid Pier gauge in recent years.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Murrells Inlet earns more in every month, with bigger homes. Pawleys Island has the most even year, with 37 percent of its income in June to August.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Summer guests book early. A typical July booking in Myrtle Beach is made in mid-May, and Murrells Inlet's July stays are booked even further ahead.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">South Carolina does not tax a stay of 90 continuous days or more by one guest as lodging. Our page on <a href="/invest/mid-term-rentals/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">mid-term rentals</a> covers renting by the month.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="costs"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="The costs">What does Airbnb take from a Myrtle Beach rental, and what else comes off?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">At AirROI's low-end cost shares, an owner-run Myrtle Beach Airbnb keeps about 63 cents of each dollar guests pay, before insurance, the HOA fee, property tax and any loan.</p><ul class="st-cost"><li><b>Airbnb's fee</b><span class="amt">15.5%</span><span class="why">Most hosts pay 15.5 percent of each booking, taken from the payout. Some still pay less on an older plan, which <a href="https://www.airbnb.com/help/article/1857" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Airbnb is phasing out</a>, so the calculator uses AirROI's average for the town.</span></li><li><b>Cleaning</b><span class="amt">about $150 a stay</span><span class="why">The guest's cleaning fee pays the cleaner, so the owner keeps none of it. It is the typical fee in Myrtle Beach.</span></li><li><b>Utilities, supplies, repairs</b><span class="amt">about 10%</span><span class="why">Utilities and internet are about half of it. Supplies, repairs and linens are the rest. Where the HOA fee pays the electric and internet, the owner does not pay most of the utilities.</span></li><li><b>Rental insurance and permit</b><span class="amt">$390 a year</span><span class="why">A short-term rental policy on top of Airbnb's free cover, and a permit where one is needed. This is AirROI's cost for Myrtle Beach; it differs by town, and the calculator fills in each town's. The owner's own condo policy is extra.</span></li><li><b>A manager, basic plan</b><span class="amt">about 13 to 17%</span><span class="why">The basic plans we have seen here cover marketing, guest messages and basic accounting. Full service adds taxes, maintenance and repairs, and is priced as a share of the profit.</span></li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The guest pays the lodging taxes on top of the price, about 13 percent inside the City of Myrtle Beach, and Airbnb collects them. Our <a href="/invest/accommodations-tax/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">accommodations tax</a> page has the rates town by town.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The worst short-term rental mistake our team sees is running it yourself with the cheapest cleaner. We have seen theft and damage follow. If you will not be here to check the cleaning, pick the manager in the calculator.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The top short-term rentals here pick one kind of guest and stay filled, such as golfers, workers or people moving here.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="more-hosts"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="More hosts">Is Myrtle Beach getting too many Airbnbs?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Myrtle Beach has many more Airbnbs than a year ago, and each new one competes with the rest for the same guests. It had 43 percent more active listings than a year earlier. Every other town in the chart grew by about a quarter or more.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="How much each town's Airbnb listings grew in a year"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">How much each town's Airbnb listings grew in a year</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Town, listings now</span><span role="columnheader">growth</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Pawleys Island</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">453 listings</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:1" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">69% more</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Murrells Inlet</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">478 listings</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.812" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">56% more</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Little River</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">169 listings</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.812" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">56% more</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Conway</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">106 listings</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.71" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">49% more</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Myrtle Beach</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">8,700 listings</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.623" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">43% more</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">North Myrtle Beach</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">4,600 listings</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.449" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">31% more</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Surfside Beach</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">551 listings</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.348" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">24% more</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>The number of active listings now, rounded. AirROI, 12 months to September 2026, compared with the year before.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Many listings book few nights. More than half of Myrtle Beach listings were booked, or blocked by their owner, 90 days or fewer in the year.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For a buyer, that means a condo should pay its bills at the nights the average listing books now. Do not plan on more.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="allowed"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Where it is allowed">Can you Airbnb a home in Myrtle Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In an oceanfront condo building, usually yes; in a house inside the city, usually not. Inside the City of Myrtle Beach, a stay under 90 days is short-term, and any rental needs a city business license. The city <a href="https://www.cityofmyrtlebeach.com/news_detail_T6_R1468.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">allows short-term stays in no residential zone</a> except RMV, the zone for apartment and condo buildings for visitors. Fewer than 30 houses in the other residential zones may still rent nightly, because they did before the zoning.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Homes for sale show the same split. Inside Myrtle Beach city limits, about 5 in 6 condos for sale are marked for nightly rentals, and few houses are. In Garden City and North Myrtle Beach, many more houses are.</p><div class="st-side" style="--r:1"><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="Houses for sale that the listing marks as allowing nightly rentals"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">Houses for sale that the listing marks as allowing nightly rentals</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Where, houses marked</span><span role="columnheader">share of houses</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Garden City area</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">38 of 51</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.745" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">75%</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">North Myrtle Beach</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">112 of 258</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.434" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">43%</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Pawleys Island</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">35 of 123</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.285" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">28%</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Surfside Beach</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">23 of 84</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.274" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">27%</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Murrells Inlet</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">34 of 206</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.165" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">17%</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Little River</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">18 of 190</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.095" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">9%</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Myrtle Beach city</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">18 of 201</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.09" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">9%</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Conway</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">34 of 675</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.05" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">5%</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>Our count of active listings, by what the listing agent entered. A listing that says nothing counts as not marked. Myrtle Beach counts only homes inside city limits. The others go by the town in the home's address, except the Garden City area, which is our own.</figcaption></figure><div class="c3-aerial c3-aerial-close"><figure class="c3ph-hero" style=""><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/buyers/no-hoa/garden-city-beach-and-marsh-from-the-ocean-2011-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/buyers/no-hoa/garden-city-beach-and-marsh-from-the-ocean-2011-600w.webp 600w, /images/buyers/no-hoa/garden-city-beach-and-marsh-from-the-ocean-2011-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1136px" width="1200" height="782" alt="Beach houses in rows between the ocean beach and a wide marsh with tidal creeks and boat docks at Garden City Beach, seen from a plane over the ocean" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.usa.gov/publicdomain/label/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: U.S. Geological Survey. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">Photo: U.S. Geological Survey</a></span></div><figcaption>Beach houses between the ocean and the marsh at Garden City Beach. In the Garden City area, about three in four houses for sale are marked for nightly rentals.</figcaption></figure></div></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem"><a href="https://www.nmb.us/833/Short-term-Rentals" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">North Myrtle Beach</a> requires a business license for every short-term rental, renewed every year, and no separate zoning or permit process. Our page on <a href="/invest/str-rules/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">short-term rental rules</a> covers each town.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A listing's mark is the listing agent's word, not the city's. Before you offer, we read the zoning for the address and the building's own rules.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Want homes where nightly stays are allowed?</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Tell us the town and your budget. We send homes for sale there and leave out the ones whose zoning or building rules ban nightly stays.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Send me homes that allow Airbnb</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="more"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="More STR pages">What else do Grand Strand Airbnb buyers ask?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Each question below has its own page.</p><style>main#main .c3-gcards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(15rem,1fr));gap:.7rem;max-width:760px;margin:.2rem 0 1rem}main#main .c3-gcard{padding:.75rem .9rem .8rem;border-radius:16px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.55);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.75);box-shadow:0 6px 18px rgba(28,32,40,.08);backdrop-filter:blur(14px) saturate(140%);-webkit-backdrop-filter:blur(14px) saturate(140%)}main#main .c3-gcard h3{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.45rem;margin:0 0 .35rem!important;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.92rem!important;font-weight:650;color:var(--navy);line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gcard h3 .i{display:inline-flex;color:var(--brass)}main#main .c3-gcard .c3-gul{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0}main#main .c3-gcard .c3-gi{font-size:.95rem;line-height:1.6;margin:0}main#main .c3-gcard a{color:var(--navy)}@media (prefers-reduced-transparency:reduce){main#main .c3-gcard{backdrop-filter:none;-webkit-backdrop-filter:none;background:#fbf8f3}}</style><div class="c3-gcards"><div class="c3-gcard"><h3><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M15 9.4c-.4-1-1.5-1.8-3-1.8-1.8 0-3 1-3 2.2 0 3 6 1.6 6 4.4 0 1.3-1.3 2.2-3 2.2-1.6 0-2.7-.7-3.1-1.8M12 5.8v1.8M12 16.4v1.8"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/></svg></span>Money</h3><ul class="c3-gul"><li class="c3-gi"><a href="/invest/airbnb-income/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">How much do Airbnbs make here?</a></li><li class="c3-gi"><a href="/invest/str-vs-ltr/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Airbnb or a yearly lease?</a></li><li class="c3-gi"><a href="/invest/rental-returns/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">What return does a rental make?</a></li><li class="c3-gi"><a href="/invest/str-tax-treatment/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">How is the income taxed?</a></li></ul></div><div class="c3-gcard"><h3><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 3h8l4 4v13a1 1 0 0 1-1 1H6a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V4a1 1 0 0 1 1-1zM14 3v4h4M9 17l6-6"/><circle cx="9.5" cy="11.5" r="1"/><circle cx="14.5" cy="16.5" r="1"/></svg></span>Rules and tax</h3><ul class="c3-gul"><li class="c3-gi"><a href="/invest/str-rules/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Where is an Airbnb allowed?</a></li><li class="c3-gi"><a href="/invest/accommodations-tax/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">What tax does the guest pay?</a></li><li class="c3-gi"><a href="/invest/14-day-rule/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">How many nights can I use it myself?</a></li></ul></div><div class="c3-gcard"><h3><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M10.8 12.2 20 3M16.8 6.2l2.5 2.5M14.3 8.7l2 2"/><circle cx="7.5" cy="15.5" r="4.5"/></svg></span>Running it</h3><ul class="c3-gul"><li class="c3-gi"><a href="/invest/str-setup/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">What do I set up after closing?</a></li><li class="c3-gi"><a href="/invest/rental-program-vs-airbnb/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Rental program or run it myself?</a></li><li class="c3-gi"><a href="/invest/mid-term-rentals/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Rent it for 90 days or more instead?</a></li><li class="c3-gi"><a href="/invest/condotel-financing/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Can I get a loan on a condotel?</a></li></ul></div></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="myrtle-beach-airbnb-questions"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Myrtle Beach Airbnb questions</h2><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Do you need a business license for an Airbnb in Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes. Inside the City of Myrtle Beach, any rental needs a city business license. North Myrtle Beach asks every short-term rental for one, renewed each year.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How much does an Airbnb make in Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The average one took in about $26,000 from guests in a year, before any cost. The chart of towns above compares eight towns by the two-bedroom average.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How many nights does a Myrtle Beach Airbnb condo need to book?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The count depends most on the HOA fee. The four typical condos in the chart above need about 42 to 110 booked nights a year to pay their bills if the owner runs them, and more with a manager.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What percentage does Airbnb take?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For most hosts, 15.5 percent of each booking. The list of costs above shows what else comes off before the HOA fee.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How much is an Airbnb cleaning fee in Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About $150 is typical. The guest pays it, and it goes to the cleaner, so the owner keeps none of it.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Who pays the lodging tax on a Myrtle Beach Airbnb?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The guest. Inside the City of Myrtle Beach the lodging taxes add about 13 percent to the price, and Airbnb collects them on stays under 90 nights.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What is the slow season for a Myrtle Beach Airbnb?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">November to February are the four slowest months. The season chart above shows each month next to the ocean's temperature.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Can you finance an Airbnb condo?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes, with limits. A loan officer at our preferred lender tells us that loans approved on the rental's income, called DSCR loans, count only about 75 percent of a short-term rental estimate. A condotel, a condo run as a hotel, needs its own kind of loan.</p><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1.6rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Sources:</strong> <a href="https://www.airroi.com/airbnb-data/united-states/south-carolina/north-myrtle-beach" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">AirROI: North Myrtle Beach</a>, <a href="https://www.airroi.com/airbnb-data/united-states/south-carolina/myrtle-beach" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Myrtle Beach</a>, <a href="https://www.airroi.com/airbnb-data/united-states/south-carolina/surfside-beach" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Surfside Beach</a>, <a href="https://www.airroi.com/airbnb-data/united-states/south-carolina/garden-city-beach" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Garden City Beach</a>, <a href="https://www.airroi.com/airbnb-data/united-states/south-carolina/murrells-inlet" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Murrells Inlet</a>, <a href="https://www.airroi.com/airbnb-data/united-states/south-carolina/pawleys-island" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Pawleys Island</a>, <a href="https://www.airroi.com/airbnb-data/united-states/south-carolina/little-river" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Little River</a>, <a href="https://www.airroi.com/airbnb-data/united-states/south-carolina/conway" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Conway</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/media/kufln4qp/tax-levy-2026_2.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">County tax levy</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t12c043.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">S.C. Code 12-43-220</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t12c036.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">S.C. Code 12-36-920</a>, <a href="https://tidesandcurrents.noaa.gov/stationhome.html?id=8661070" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NOAA Springmaid Pier</a>, <a href="https://dor.sc.gov/sites/dor/files/forms/ST575.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SCDOR ST-575</a>, <a href="https://www.airbnb.com/help/article/1857" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Airbnb host fees</a>, <a href="https://www.airbnb.com/help/article/2328" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Airbnb taxes</a>, <a href="https://www.cityofmyrtlebeach.com/news_detail_T6_R1468.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">City zoning</a>, <a href="https://www.nmb.us/833/Short-term-Rentals" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">North Myrtle Beach rentals</a>. Airbnb: AirROI, 12 months to September 2026; months, the last two years. Homes for sale: our count of active listings. Our arithmetic. Not legal or tax advice.</p><div class="c3ph-credits"><div class="c3ph-h" id="photo-credits">Photo credits</div><div role="list" aria-labelledby="photo-credits"><div role="listitem">Oceanfront towers in Myrtle Beach, with streets of houses behind them, seen from over the ocean. Photo: U.S. Geological Survey, <a href="https://www.usa.gov/publicdomain/label/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://doi.org/10.5066/F7N877XX" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">U.S. Geological Survey</a>. Chapter3 Realty cropped and resized the photo.</div><div role="listitem">Beach houses between the ocean and the marsh at Garden City Beach. Photo: U.S. Geological Survey, <a href="https://www.usa.gov/publicdomain/label/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://doi.org/10.5066/F7N877XX" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">U.S. Geological Survey</a>.</div><div role="listitem">Chapter3 Realty resized these photos and cropped some of them.</div></div></div><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"ImageObject","contentUrl":"https://chapter3realty.com/images/2026-10-d/invest-str-tools/myrtle-beach-oceanfront-towers-and-houses-2011-1200w.webp","url":"https://chapter3realty.com/images/2026-10-d/invest-str-tools/myrtle-beach-oceanfront-towers-and-houses-2011-1200w.webp","width":1200,"height":675,"encodingFormat":"image/webp","name":"Oceanfront towers in Myrtle Beach, with streets of houses behind them, seen